{"id": "sonnet__GEN__omni_2056__0", "result": "We need 100A+10B+C = B^C \u2212 A, so 101A+10B+C = B^C, with A \u2265 1.\n\nSearch over B (2 to 9), C (0 to 9):\n\n- B=2: 2^C \u2264 512, but we need at least 101+... \u2265 101. 2^7=128: 101A+20+7=128 \u2192 101A=101 \u2192 A=1. So 127 is a candidate: check 2^7 \u2212 1 = 127. \u2713.\n\nCheck others for uniqueness:\n- B=3: 3^5=243: 101A+30+5=243 \u2192 101A=208, no. 3^6=729: 101A=729\u221236=693, no (101\u00b76=606, 101\u00b77=707). 3^4=81 is too small.\n- B=4: 4^4=256: 101A=256\u221244=212, no. 4^5=1024 is too large (max is 999+... 101\u00b79+90+9=1008, so it's possible: 1024\u221245=979, no).\n- B=5: 5^3=125: 101A=125\u221253=72, no. 5^4=625: 625\u221254=571, no.\n- B=6: 6^3=216: 216\u221263=153, no. 6^4=1296 is too large.\n- B=7: 7^3=343: 343\u221273=270, no. 7^4 is too large.\n- B=8: 8^3=512: 512\u221283=429, no. \n- B=9: 9^3=729: 729\u221293=636, no (101\u00b76=606). \n- B=1 or 0: B^C \u2264 1, impossible.\n\nThe only solution is 127.\n\nANSWER: 127", "rc": 0, "cost": 0.01097, "model_used": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "secs": 13.6}